From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:05:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/27] sycl : let MTP draft graphs replay with a quantized
 draft KV

A quantized KV cache adds Hadamard rotation matmuls whose row count is
tokens x heads x dim/64. The graph cache's token limit read that as a
token count, so every draft and catch-up graph of an MTP context with
a q8_0 KV ran eagerly. GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_ROT_ROWS=1 (default off) leaves
FWHT-served rotation matmuls out of that test. Adds a too_big reason
line to GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_STATS and head-count options to the host
harnesses.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
